From: SAGIT Port <sagit@local>
Subject: [PATCH] sagit: keep the VM page size at 4K

arm_init advertises 16K VM pages on every arm64 device with more than 1GB
of RAM.  SAGIT uses 4K hardware page tables, so that choice produces
PAGE_RATIO=4 and makes write_pte_fast require 32-byte-aligned PTE groups
while the rest of this port uses native 4K mappings.  Keep the VM page size
equal to ARM_PGSHIFT on SAGIT; other boards retain the original policy.
---
 osfmk/arm/arm_init.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/osfmk/arm/arm_init.c b/osfmk/arm/arm_init.c
--- a/osfmk/arm/arm_init.c
+++ b/osfmk/arm/arm_init.c
@@ -398,6 +398,10 @@ arm_init(
 		/*
 		 * Select the advertised kernel page size.
 		 */
+#if defined(SAGIT)
+		/* SAGIT uses native 4K VM pages as well as 4K hardware page tables. */
+		PAGE_SHIFT_CONST = ARM_PGSHIFT;
+#else
 		if (args->memSize > 1ULL * 1024 * 1024 * 1024) {
 			/*
 			 * arm64 device with > 1GB of RAM:
@@ -413,6 +417,7 @@ arm_init(
 			 */
 			PAGE_SHIFT_CONST = ARM_PGSHIFT;
 		}
+#endif
 
 		/* 32-bit apps always see 16KB page size */
 		page_shift_user32 = PAGE_MAX_SHIFT;
